    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d693">

                <pb facs="0649" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg637"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/11–1744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Henderson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-17T18:00:00+03:00">November 17,
                            1944—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 23—11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>251. Tahsin Qadri, Iraqi Minister at Beirut now in Baghdad, told me today that
                    the new Soviet Minister to Syria and the Lebanon<anchor n="56" xml:id="d693-f1"
                    /> has told him in confidence that the Soviet Government is unqualifiedly
                    opposed to the Zionist program. ReDept’s circular infotel November 14, 6 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">10</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d693-f2"/> Wadsworth
                    is undoubtedly in a better position than I to evaluate the reliability of the
                    Iraqi Minister.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Beirut.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henderson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d693-f1" n="56" xml:id="d693-f1-content">
                <p>Daniil Semenovich Solod.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d693-f2" n="57" xml:id="d693-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. In reply to an inquiry from the Department, the Minister to Syria
                    and Lebanon (Wadsworth) in telegram 277, December 6, 4 p.m., stated that he had
                    been informed by the Iraqi Minister that the Soviet Minister had told him that
                    the Soviet Union would do nothing to support Zionism. Mr. Wadsworth expressed
                    confidence in the Iraqi Minister’s statement.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
